  {
    "id": "ssa",
    "repo": "danielep71/K-FRTB-SSA",
    "status": "No version has been released. The repository holds a prototype of the calculation, which has not been compiled or run in Excel: Calculation: Prototype. The VBA source of a MAR40 engine for the four risk classes is under src/, with a macro-free template of 18 sheets and synthetic sample data: the prototype says what it calculates, how to use and build it and what it does not do, and the workbook contract defines its layout. I have run it only in LibreOffice's VBA mode: it is not compiled or run in Excel, no evidence of a run is recorded here, and it is not validated for regulatory reporting. Methodology: The Basel Framework's chapter MAR40 is the registered source, and each calculation of the engine has a contract whose rules cite it, with every parameter compared with the text. The data contract defines every input field and how a cell is read. No rule is validated. Test cases: 20 cases cover the seven calculations: the sample portfolio, limits and invalid rows. Three hold values published in MAR40 and in the Basel Committee's 2005 update of its 1996 market risk amendment; the others are derived within the project and validate nothing. The workbook's VBA tests are four suites of the test harness, with a certification entry point each; one of them, generated from the cases, runs all 20 in the workbook, and one probes what the workbook relies on Excel to do. They have run only in LibreOffice: no case has run in Excel. Tooling and governance: In use: every change goes through a pull request that Repository integrity checks. The release state is recorded in one place: the Current status of RELEASING.md, which Repository integrity checks against CHANGELOG.md. Changes reach main through task branches and pull requests; only a release is versioned and tagged.",
